{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB13762 - MONDO_7186",
  "verbalization": "Dexrabeprazole is implicated in the pathogenesis of Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease (GERD) through a multi-step pathway involving Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome and Esomeprazole. The evidence suggests that Dexrabeprazole, through its indication for Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome, indirectly contributes to GERD by promoting the production of gastric acid, which is a key factor in GERD development. This is further supported by the indication of Dexrabeprazole for Hyperinsulinism, which may have a secondary role in the pathophysiology of GERD, though its direct contribution remains less clear. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role of Dexrabeprazole in GERD through its involvement in acid secretion and related conditions, though the exact mechanism and extent of its contribution require further investigation.",
